#### Article 4

1. The objectives of protection for women victims of violence are directed to:a. create conditions that support the development of the potential of women victims of violence;  
b. strengthen the potential already possessed by women victims of violence; andc. improve the work skills of women victims of violence.  
2. The objectives of protection for child victims of violence are directed to:a. provide social rehabilitation for child victims of violence;  
b. reunite child victims of violence with their family and/or environment; andc. improve the empowerment of child victims of violence.

# CHAPTER III

## PROTECTION OF WOMEN

## VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

## Part One

Stages

#### Article 5

The stages of protection for women victims of violence include: a. prevention of violence against women;  
b. protection services for women victims of violence; and c. empowerment of women victims of violence.

## Part Two

Implementation

### Paragraph 1

Prevention of Violence Against Women

#### Article 6

1. Prevention of violence against women as referred to in Article 5 letter a is carried out in an integrated manner coordinated by the Regional Apparatus in charge of women's empowerment and child protection.  
2. Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by involving:a. family;  
b. community;  
c. private sector;  
d. community institutions;  
e. social institutions; andf. educational institutions.

#### Article 7

Prevention of violence against women as referred to in Article 6 is implemented among others by: a. forming a network in efforts to prevent violence against women;  
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns with the community, private sector and non-governmental organizations; andc. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of women.

### Paragraph 2

Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence

#### Article 8

1. Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in Article 5 letter b are provided to women residents of the Region and/or women who experience violence with the location of the incident in the Region.  
2. The implementation of Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out with the principles of:a. fast;  
b. safe;  
c. sense of empathy;  
d. non-discrimination;  
e. easily accessible; andf. guaranteed confidentiality.

#### Article 9

1. The forms of Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in Article 8 include:a. legal aid services;  
b. health services;  
c. social rehabilitation services;  
d. repatriation and social reintegration services;  
e. complaint, consultation, and counseling services; and/or f. assistance services.  
2. In addition to Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1), Services are carried out by receiving and sending case referrals from/or to other service units in a networked manner.  
3. The implementation of Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by the Regional Apparatus in charge of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.  
4. Further provisions regarding the forms and procedures of Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) through (3) are regulated by Mayor Regulation.

### Paragraph 3

Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence

#### Article 10

1. Empowerment of women victims of violence as referred to in Article 5 letter c is implemented through efforts including:a. job training; andb. productive economic enterprises and joint business groups. (2) The implementation of empowerment of women victims of violence is carried out with the principles of:a. equality and fairness of rights;  
b. responsibility;  
c. efficiency and effectiveness; andd. respect and enforcement of human rights. (3) The implementation of empowerment of women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by related Regional Apparatus in accordance with their main duties and functions.

# CHAPTER IV

## PROTECTION OF CHILD VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

## Part One

Stages

#### Article 11

The stages of protection for child victims of violence include: a. prevention of violence against children;  
b. handling of child victims of violence; andc. rehabilitation of child victims of violence.

## Part Two

Implementation

### Paragraph 1

Prevention of Violence against Children

#### Article 12

1. Prevention of Violence against Children as referred to in Article 11 letter a is implemented by:a. forming a network in efforts to Prevent Violence against Children;  
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of Violence Prevention based on partnership patterns with the community, private sector and Non-Governmental Organizations; andc. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the Protection of Child Victims of Violence.  
2. Prevention of Violence against Children as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out in an integrated manner and coordinated by the Regional Apparatus in charge of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

#### Article 13

Efforts to prevent Violence against Children as referred to in Article 12 are carried out by involving: a. parents and/or family;  
b. community;  
c. educational institutions;  
d. child social welfare institutions; and/ore. other institutions engaged in child protection care.

### Paragraph 2

Handling of Child Victims of Violence

#### Article 14

1. Handling of child victims of violence as referred to in Article 11 letter b is implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
2. In handling child victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may cooperate with:a. vertical agencies;  
b. provincial government;  
c. other regency/city governments;  
d. village government;  
e. non-governmental organizations;  
f. private parties;  
g. community; and/orh. family.

### Paragraph 3

Rehabilitation of Child Victims of Violence

#### Article 15

1. Rehabilitation Services for Child Victims of Violence as referred to in Article 11 letter c are carried out in the form of: a. legal aid services;  
b. health rehabilitation services;  
c. social rehabilitation services; and/ord. repatriation and social reintegration services.  
2. In the Rehabilitation services for Child Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the City Regional Government may cooperate with:a. vertical agencies;  
b. provincial government;  
c. other regency/city governments;  
d. village government;  
e. non-governmental organizations;  
f. private parties;  
g. community; and/orh. family.  
3. Further provisions regarding the forms and procedures of rehabilitation services for Child Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated in a Mayor Regulation.

# CHAPTER V

## RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

#### Article 16

1. Every Victim has the right to:a. the right to have their dignity respected as a human being;  
b. the right to health and psychological recovery;  
c. the right to determine their own decisions;  
d. the right to obtain information;  
e. the right to confidentiality of identity;  
f. the right to compensation from the perpetrator;  
g. the right to Social Rehabilitation;  
h. the right to complaint handling;  
i. the right to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and/orj. the right to assistance.  
2. In addition to the rights as referred to in paragraph (1), Child Victims of Violence have the right to:a. the right to respect for the continuity of life, growth and development;  
b. the right to basic services;  
c. the right to equal protection;  
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/ore. the right to obtain freedom.
